body:
Slice 2 of 5 of #637. Depends on #654 (the record types) and #661 (same-file ordering in `gc.rs`).

## What

- `ReferenceSet` gains the disjoint staged set: committed `part:` fragments and in-flight owned `sidx:` fragments, built by bounded per-session ranges; `protects()` gains the pending `retire:bytes:` class; the expiry arm is unchanged (it scans only `pending:`, which no longer holds owned entries);
- reclamation intent precedes fragment destruction: the sweep CASes `orphan:<pos>` to `reclaiming` and commits before `delete_fragment`, deleting the key afterwards as today — the ordering the adoption CAS's precondition depends on;
- all three `orphan:` value variants (legacy bare decimal, `{ orphaned_at_millis, event }`, `{ ..., reclaiming: true }`) decode, never reject;
- the fragment-less mark sweep (positions no `list_fragments()` reported, aged past `W_repoint + W_write + delta_clock`, observed absent after that deadline).

## Acceptance

- staged fragments survive a GC pass, asserted by a positive observable (the drain answer for a server holding them), not a vacuous "nothing was deleted";
- intent-before-destruction ordering asserted; all three variants decoded;
- `cargo xtask ci` green.

Part of #637 / #508 / epic #513.
